  "prompt": "[system]\n\n    You generate compact, robust Python TSP metaheuristics.\n    You must follow the requested interface exactly, always preserve tour validity.\n    \n\n[user]\nPARENTS:\nCandidate cand_000007: farthest_insertion_2opt\n\nStatus: timeout; distance: 8.28989\n\nThought: Construct tour via farthest-insertion heuristic, then apply 2-opt local search to intensify exploitation. Repeatedly reverses segments to eliminate crossings until no improvement. Reports best tour after construction and after each improvement.\n\nError details: timeout on tsp_construct_100_seed2024_007: Solver timed out after 30.002s (timeout_seconds=30)\n\nHistory source: yes\nHistory bucket: tsp:size:100\nHistory role: regime specialist\n\nCode:\n\n```python\n\nimport numpy as np\ndef solve_tsp(distance_matrix: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n    n = len(distance_matrix)\n    if n <= 2:\n        tour = np.arange(n)\n        report_best_tour(tour)\n        return tour\n    # Farthest insertion construction\n    start = 0\n    end = np.argmax(distance_matrix[start])\n    tour = [start, end]\n    in_tour = {start, end}\n    while len(tour) < n:\n        best_node = -1\n        best_dist = -1.0\n        for node in range(n):\n            if node in in_tour:\n                continue\n            min_dist = min(distance_matrix[node][t] for t in tour)\n            if min_dist > best_dist:\n                best_dist = min_dist\n                best_node = node\n        best_pos = -1\n        best_increase = float('inf')\n        for i in range(len(tour)):\n            a = tour[i]\n            b = tour[(i+1)%len(tour)]\n            increase = distance_matrix[a][best_node] + distance_matrix[best_node][b] - distance_matrix[a][b]\n            if increase < best_increase:\n                best_increase = increase\n                best_pos = i+1\n        tour.insert(best_pos, best_node)\n        in_tour.add(best_node)\n    tour = np.array(tour)\n    report_best_tour(tour)\n    # 2-opt improvement\n    improved = True\n    while improved:\n        improved = False\n        for i in range(n-2):\n            for j in range(i+2, n):\n                # edges (i,i+1) and (j,(j+1)%n)\n                a = tour[i]\n                b = tour[(i+1)%n]\n                c = tour[j]\n                d = tour[(j+1)%n]\n                delta = distance_matrix[a][c] + distance_matrix[b][d] - distance_matrix[a][b] - distance_matrix[c][d]\n                if delta < 0:\n                    # reverse segment i+1..j\n                    tour[i+1:j+1] = tour[i+1:j+1][::-1]\n                    improved = True\n                    report_best_tour(tour)\n                    break  # restart from beginning\n            if improved:\n                break\n    return tour\n\n```\n\nVERBAL GRADIENT: follow the reflection below as the primary source of change.\n\nUse the supplied parents as supporting evidence only.\n\nPARENT-SPECIFIC LLM REFLECTIONS:\n\nParent cand_000007 LLM reflection:\n- Summary: Farthest-insertion with 2-opt improved tour length but incurred 5 timeouts, violating timeout constraint.\n- Aim: Eliminate timeouts while maintaining or improving tour quality, e.g., by adding an iteration limit or runtime check to 2-opt.\n- Preserve: farthest-insertion construction; report_best_tour after construction and after each improvement; basic 2-opt segment reversal logic\n- Change: Add a runtime check or iteration limit to the 2-opt loop to guarantee timely completion; Optionally break 2-opt early if no improvement after a few passes\n- Avoid: Removing 2-opt altogether; Degrading construction quality; Introducing invalid tour permutations\n\nDistance is the search objective for TSP; lower distance is better.\n\nImplement a complete TSP metaheuristic inside this required entrypoint:\n\ndef solve_tsp(distance_matrix: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n\nRequirements:\n- Minimize total TSP tour distance.\n- Return a 1D np.ndarray containing each node exactly once.\n- Do not repeat t